---
import PropertyPackPage from '@/components/property-pack/PropertyPackPage.astro';
import { candidateManifest } from '@/lib/property-pack-model.mjs';
---
<PropertyPackPage
  title="Later review and releases"
  description="How later working-group review, controlled change and immutable versions follow the accelerated Property Pack technical determination."
  category="Review and versioning"
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Later review and releases' }]}
>
  <h1>Later review and releases</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The accepted sequence starts with a recorded Technical Working Group determination,
    then allows later domain, scheme and Interoperability review. No initial determination
    is recorded here. This page explains how later changes would preserve the evidence
    and the version that was actually reviewed.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--note">
    <p class="callout__label">Current state</p>
    <p>
      Candidate <code>{candidateManifest.candidate_version}</code> is not determined or
      released. No later working-group review, implementation release or external
      authority decision is recorded.
    </p>
  </div>


  <h2 id="sequence">Review sequence</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Record the Technical Working Group determination against an immutable candidate digest.</li>
    <li>Identify the ontology areas owned or consumed by each later working group.</li>
    <li>Collect evidence, questions and proposed dispositions without rewriting the determined baseline.</li>
    <li>Assess cross-context and implementation impact through Governance and Interoperability.</li>
    <li>Publish an explicit new candidate or release only after its own authority gate passes.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="change-control">Controlled change</h2>
  <p>
    A later proposal must identify the affected source items and ontology constructs,
    cite evidence, name the semantic owner, state compatibility impact and record its
    disposition. Accepted changes create a new version; they do not edit the evidence
    used for an earlier determination in place.
  </p>

  <h2 id="version-contract">Version contract</h2>
  <dl class="v2-facts">
    <div><dt>Current source cut</dt><dd><code>{candidateManifest.candidate_version}</code> under <code>source/03-standards/ontology-candidates/property-pack/0.1/</code></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Determined version</dt><dd>Not yet assigned</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Later revision</dt><dd>Must receive a distinct identifier, change record and validation receipt</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Compatibility</dt><dd>Must be assessed explicitly; no silent replacement of PDTF schema contracts</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h2 id="claims">Claims that remain separate</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Technical checks passing does not mean semantic agreement.</li>
    <li>A Technical Working Group determination does not mean every domain group has reviewed the model.</li>
    <li>A determined ontology component is not automatically an implementation release or adopted SPDTF standard.</li>
    <li>Use in government-scheme work does not itself grant OPDA statutory or delegated authority.</li>
  </ul>
</PropertyPackPage>
